# Go sources are LF in the repository and have to be LF in every checkout.
#
# `gofmt -l .` is a CI gate here, and gofmt reports a CRLF file as unformatted. Windows checks text
# files out with CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true), so without this rule that gate failed on that
# platform for every file at once — a platform-shaped failure that says nothing about the code. An
# `eol` attribute overrides core.autocrlf, and the rule only pins the working tree: the blobs are LF
# already, so no file in the repository changes.
*.go text eol=lf
